{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, avgpool) is the best result so far at 0.591 acc, showing multiprofile aggregation is a major gain over singleprofile (0.485). Config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, concat) showed that adding resnet50 image features to RNA provides a modest but consistent boost (+0.042 over config_001). Uncertainty: it is unclear whether the image modality's benefit transfers to the multiprofile setting, or whether the stronger RNA signal in multiprofile makes the weak image contribution redundant. Config_018 tests exactly this: it keeps the proven multiprofile+avgpool+pca_n2000 backbone from config_002 and adds resnet50 with concat fusion (the same fusion that worked in config_016), changing only the modality composition. This is the most informative next step because (a) it directly extends the two strongest findings, (b) it isolates the effect of adding image to the multiprofile context, and (c) the result will clarify whether further multimodal experiments (transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, ViT) are worth pursuing or whether the multiprofile RNA signal is already near its ceiling."
}

